{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0250", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-flat-morphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af3ee0add1b87ef4c578021012ad4379236e59f1649c0db1d044904e5b77ca08", "source_text": "Flat morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5101da78695397f71e6c1c92f94f5a64eb3a82dc54967e2fa50174e71f2980d7", "unit_id": "tag:0250:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0250", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:700ba248d32ddc6bd19af161e604216a68972c9a9d8a7d139ca2d879ea41069f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section simply exists to summarize the properties of flatness that will\nbe useful to us. Thus, we will be content with stating the theorems precisely\nand giving references for the proofs.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nAfter briefly recalling the necessary facts about flat modules over Noetherian\nrings, we state a theorem of Grothendieck which gives sufficient conditions\nfor ``hyperplane sections'' of certain modules to be flat.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dc889030258cf0c08543a8fb5a8eba2cec5ca8a8776c26fe6dc3d44c411115bb", "unit_id": "tag:0250:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0250", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$N$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$M \\mapsto M \\otimes_A N$", "MATH_0004": "$N$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$f : A \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$M \\mapsto M \\otimes_A B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-flat-rings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5b6f649ff43552c10978313fc86ad0963a686c882cbbc130fec75522669d9775", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cca1e1e32cf6955782da76092df1fe397bacaa86c382af996c28444ec4f617fb", "source_text": "Flatness of modules and rings.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A module <MATH_0001> over a ring <MATH_0002> is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>flat<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif the functor <MATH_0003> is exact.\n<STRUCT_0003> If this functor is also faithful, we say that\n<MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>faithfully flat<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> over <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004> A morphism of rings <MATH_0006> is said to be\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>flat (resp. faithfully flat)<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nif the functor <MATH_0007> is exact\n(resp. faithful and exact).\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8e90c8daa9df51409e1ff15781c672965067ce02d761e16b32632f13ea53ce7", "unit_id": "tag:0251:statement"}
